WEBVTT

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.000
I-It's a witch's store...

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.850
The population of Kumade Village

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.400
has been decreasing rapidly lately,

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.770
and we're clearly facing depopulation.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:17.820
In order for us to revitalize and
develop our village however we can,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:22.660
I'd like to hear young people's opinions and ideas,

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.160
Why are we having the meeting here today?

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:28.080
and ask Master Natsu to choose which to pursue.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.790
That's why. You see?

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.370
So... Firstly,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.290
Kumade Village is—

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.090
So how will we know if we've succeeded?

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.590
Maybe we'll have lots of tourists?

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.090
Hm... Tourists, huh?

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.600
Kumade Village doesn't have any places that can attract tourists.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.600
You're too negative, Miss Yasuda!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.100
Nooo!

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.100
Even if we don't have any places to
attract them, we can just make some!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.730
We'll have tourists, especially young people, visit here.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.730
If they click "like" on Kumade Village using their phones and computers,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.200
we'll have more tourists!

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.740
But what kinds of places do young people go to?

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.870
Well, I bet they like to go shopping, and to amusement parks and stuff.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.120
We're not asking your opinion, Matsu.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.670
We should take this opportunity to ask the young people here.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.800
Well, Mr. Sakata's daughter... Hibiki, was it?

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.260
What kind of places do young people go to on their days off?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.470
Well, places like Ville-Van.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.560
Huh?

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:27.390
Bulle...?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:28.060
Bulle-ban?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.020
Vi... Vui...?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.180
Ban-ban?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.850
No... It's Village Vanguard!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.440
Bulle...?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.110
Bullege Ban?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.520
Bullege Bingard?

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.530
By the way, what kind of place is that?

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.410
It's sorta like a combination of a general store and a bookstore

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.700
Then we can check out that store

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.960
and make Kumade Village like Billegan Buard.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.040
Village Vanguard, that is.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.340
Well, I've never been there,
so I don't know anything about it.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.010
Well then, Machi.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:01.720
Yes?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.630
Could you go check it out?

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.550
Huh?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.850
That store... you know...

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.390
Oh, right.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.140
Velgian Giangurd.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.810
Village Vanguard.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:11.810
What?

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.190
That's a good idea!

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.810
Yep, let's do it.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.020
What?!

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:22.280
Yep!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.990
Your mission this time is...

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.750
Go buy a DVD on Pythagorean Devices at Ville-Van.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.460
So she's really gonna do it?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.420
Isn't it a bit difficult for her?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.420
She'll have to ride both a train and a bus, right?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.250
Then you take her to the store, Yoshio.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.880
Still, it's a place with lots people and stores.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.390
I think this is a good opportunity for both the village and Machi.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.480
High school girls from the countryside

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.480
even go to places like that on their way home from school.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:59.400
Even if you have to take a bus,
that's the place you have to go.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.490
Well, going to a book store might be
easier for Machi than a clothing store.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.030
The store is popular amoung middle school students, too.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:08.870
In any case, this is basically Machi running an errand for you, right?

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.330
Why Pythagorean Devices?

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.450
I started wanting one for some reason.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:16.080
That place definitely is full of inexplicably tempting stuff.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.340
Village Vanguard?

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.210
Don't panic, Machi.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.630
Make full use of your knowledge, and think...

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.470
"Village" is a community like Kumade.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.970
"Vanguard"...

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:33.980
I sort of remember that it means "the world created by humans."

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.360
In short, it's a village!

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.070
You're wrong.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.490
Well, it's an unusual bookstore.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.570
Oh, it's a bookstore?

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.830
Well, you'll understand when you get there.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.810
Don't get lost, okay?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.730
Village Vanguard is...

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.440
Looks like it's on the third floor.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.360
Let's use the escalator.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.210
I'm too close to him!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.750
But there's someone behind me!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:45.630
By the way, Ma—

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.380
Oh, sorry.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.380
But why are you standing so close to me?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.310
Yoshio! Yoshio!

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.480
This is amazing! This place is huge!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.980
There are so many people!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.820
They have so many cute things!

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:48.610
They sure do.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.820
Why don't you go check it out?

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:55.370
What?!

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.160
Well... I can't do that...

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:58.950
Why not?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.200
Because...

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.170
Please go ahead and take a look!

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.880
For example, that store lady...

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.380
I work at this cute, stylish store.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:12.880
I want these girls to have a wonderful shopping experience as always.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:14.260
But...

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.770
I don't want an unfashionable
girl to come to my stylish store.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.940
Are you looking for something specific?

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.190
That's what she'll think!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.730
I don't think she will.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.860
Even if she did, you could just ignore that.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.780
Forget it! I'll go to a store like
that after I become fashionable!

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:37.780
Hm?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:40.950
We're here!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:51.880
I-It's a witch's store...

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.590
See? It's an interesting store, isn't it?

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.390
This is different from what I imagined.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.560
This isn't a bookstore...

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.810
What're you doing? Hurry up and go inside.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.520
What?! Wait! I can't! I can't! I can't!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.810
Why? After coming all this way...

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.570
Because it's a stylish store!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.150
Their ceiling is black and they use indirect lighting!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.450
No one's wearing a school uniform in there!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.650
Yeah, it's a holiday today, so...

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.360
Now, go on.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:18.870
No! No! No!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:19.780
It's embarrassing!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.660
It'll be fine! It'll be fine!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.660
It won't be fine!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.870
But you know, us doing this in
front of the store is making a scene.

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.040
Everyone's watching us.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.170
A school uniform...

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.170
A school uniform...

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.550
A school uniform...

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:40.050
I bet she doesn't have stylish clothes.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.050
A school uniform...

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.260
A school uniform...

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.050
A school uniform...

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.930
She's a country girl!

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.190
Machi?

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.400
Machi!

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.790
Hick! Country bumpkin!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.830
<i>Please do not play around the
escalators under any circumstances.</i>

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:13.000
<i>It is very dangerous to let small
children use the escalators alone.</i>

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.670
<i>If you are with them, please
make sure to hold their hands.</i>

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.560
You shouldn't be playing in a place like this.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.480
Are you lost?

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.570
I'm... sorry...

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.420
Well, it was quite an ordeal... And painful....

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.590
Where's my DVD?

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.800
She couldn't even go into the store.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.510
That's a total failure, then.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.680
Don't be so hard on her. She's still young.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.720
How pathetic...

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.680
On top of that, she was a bother for others.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:13.940
I didn't realize that her bumpkin
complex and shyness were this bad.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:17.940
It was good that a nice person
noticed your child identification tag.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:22.910
If you didn't have it, he would have taken you to the lost child center, Machi.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:26.700
The fact that she even has one is already embarrassing enough.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.620
Good grief...

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:36.210
Maybe you should rethink going to school in the city.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.670
You think this turned out terribly too, right, Yoshio?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:41.590
Hm? Well...

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.600
Wasn't it your fault this time, Natsu?

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.560
What?

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.350
Machi wasn't ready to handle all that.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.100
Machi does things at her own pace, so don't push her.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:57.780
Natsu, even though you're a bear,
you shouldn't be so firm with people.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:03.070
Just because you can do something doesn't mean you can blame others for not being able to.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.620
I'm sorry.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.620
See, Machi? Natsu is apologizing.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.790
Machi! I'm sorry!

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.750
I won't blame you anymore, so stop crying! Okay?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.430
Yoshio! Machi is...

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.010
Okay, Natsu! Kneel! Kneel and apologize!

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.400
Machi! Look at me! I'm kneeling down!

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.080
Natsu!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.420
Roar!

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.430
Roar!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:07.930
Roar!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.100
Don't worry, Natsu! It's just a teething fever.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.980
A lot happened today, so I bet she's just exhausted.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.060
She'll be fine once she gets some rest.

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.310
It's my fault!

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.860
Roar!

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.820
I'm more worried about him.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.490
Don't worry, Natsu. Machi wasn't mad, right?

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.580
But... But...

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.000
Roar!

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:36.170
Machi, I'll ask my mom to make you dinner, okay?

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.340
It's fine. I'll make it myself.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:44.090
Okay, then you can eat with Natsu, right?

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.890
Well, I'm sure they'll be fine.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.930
Kumaaa!

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.400
Kumaaa!

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:03.610
Kumaaa... Kumaaa...

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:03.530
Machi's Room

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.860
Kumaaan... Kumaaan...

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:14.700
Machi, it's dinner time, so you should come out of you room.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.010
Machi...

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.430
What should I do to help you feel better?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.390
Grandma... Grandma...

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.520
What do I do, Grandma?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.270
Natsu feels sick.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.280
Natsu, are you okay?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.030
Get better soon.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.860
Natsu, this is rice porridge.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:28.570
Have some.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.590
Natsu...

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.380
Get better soon.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:55.100
Natsu! I'm glad you're all better now!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:57.930
I'm so glad!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:05.110
I'm really glad...

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:22.290
Oh boy...

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:26.210
Okay!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:27.750
I'm gonna make rice porridge.

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:49.480
This will do.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.280
I guess I'll make something else as well.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.740
What can I make?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.200
We have vegetables.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.740
We have meat, too.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:03.460
No... it might be a bit too difficult for me...

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.130
But maybe I'll see what I can do.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.250
Pork miso soup!

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.260
It tastes okay... I guess.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.380
What're you doing, Natsu?

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:58.510
Ah, Machi!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.760
Dinner's ready!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.770
How're you feeling? Can you eat?

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:05.770
Yeah.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:11.270
Since we have vegetables and stuff,
I thought I'd at least make miso soup.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:15.780
Holding the knife was really tough!

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:17.860
And you know, Machi...

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.040
I feel really bad about what I said earlier.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.300
Everyone has things they aren't good at.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:38.300
I'm sorry for forcing you to do
something you couldn't handle.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.600
I'm sorry for saying mean things to you.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.640
Natsu...

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.270
It's not your fault.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:50.850
It's my fault for not being able to do
normal things that everyone else can.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.400
But... But...

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:58.110
Come on... Don't worry about it. It wasn't your fault.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:00.950
So cheer up. Okay?

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.700
Machi...

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.950
She's being considerate to someone like me...

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.410
She sure has grown up...

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.840
That's right... It's my fault.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.460
I can't even go clothes shopping by myself.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:20.050
I went the wrong direction on the escalator, too.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.260
It's my...

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.560
It's nothing... It's nothing...

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.600
I shouldn't be discouraged by things like this, right?

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:38.150
Humans grow by making mistakes
like this and learning from them, right?

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:42.860
I'll experience more embarrassing things from now on, right?

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.570
Yes, yes, yes!

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:48.870
Yeah... and when I become an adult...

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:52.620
they'll all become cute memories.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.670
Wait! What're you doing?

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.800
Lemme go! Lemme do it!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.460
Control yourself!

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:03.550
No! Don't go flipping tables like they do in anime and stuff!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.760
People will think that you're a strange girl!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.760
You're embarrassing yourself even more!

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:09.470
You stupid Natsu!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.140
Ow! Ow!

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:12.770
You don't even know how embarrassed I was!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:12.770
Ow! Ow!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:14.560
That's right...

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.070
When you get down to it, it's all my fault.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.940
As long as Machi feels better...

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:25.070
I don't care how much of a beating I have to take...

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:29.240
because this is my atonement.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.870
I'm sorry, Machi.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.790
You were embarrassed, right?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.540
It hurts, right?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.790
It suffocating, right?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.250
It's unbearable, right?

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.470
Machi... I'm sorry...

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.550
I'm sorry!

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:49.640
Machi!

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.730
Good morning!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:56.610
Hm?

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:03.030
I'm glad you're looking better, Machi!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.280
Breakfast is great!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.530
You look sleepy, Natsu.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:07.450
Yeah...

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.200
Machi went wild last night...

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.120
battering me...

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.040
Are you okay, Natsu? You don't look well.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.510
You should always get a good night's sleep.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:22.460
Yeah...

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:25.680
Well then, I'm going to school.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.720
Natsu, we'll perform kagura today,

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:31.680
so make sure you're in good shape by the time I come home, okay?

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.140
Kuma...

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:35.690
See you later!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.730
Good day...

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:39.860
It must've been quite the ordeal, Natsu.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:48.320
Yeah... But I'm glad that Machi feels better now.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.620
Natsu!

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:29.340
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:33.890
Hm? What? You're hungry?

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:36.640
Well, if I remember correctly...

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:40.270
We have the BBQ flavored one.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.020
Soak...

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:48.280
She's melting each one in her mouth before chewing.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:48.940
Soak...

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:54.200
Kumaaamikooo~i.
